<title>USA: USDA halves North Korea corn production estimate.</title>
<headline>USDA halves North Korea corn production estimate.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department has reduced its estimate for North Korean corn production to one million tonnes from two million tonnes, a top USDA analyst said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Gerald Bange, chairman of USDA's outlook board, told USDA Radio the forecast was lowered &quot;primarily because of information that we have which indicates that about half of North Korea's corn acreage was in fact consumed as a food item as opposed to being used for field corn production.&quot;</p>
<p>After two years of floods, North Korea is in economic ruin and appealing for international aid to stave off famine.</p>
</text>
